   "text": {
    "L1": "A sequence is a list of numbers made by a rule.",
    "L2": "The first two terms do not decide the whole sequence. The rule must work for every term.",
    "L3": "Odd numbers start at 1 and add 2 each time. Even numbers start at 2 and also add 2.",
    "L4": "Triangular numbers use growing additions: add 1, then 2, then 3, then 4.",
    "L5": "Square numbers are n times n, so the sequence is 1, 4, 9, 16, 25.",
    "L6": "Cube numbers are n times n times n. Powers of 2 double each time.",
    "L7": "Saying the rule in words helps you find any term, without listing every earlier term.",
    "L8": "Now use the odd-number rule to choose the next two terms after 11."
   },
